    "articles": [
      {
        "sequence_id": 1,
        "text": "D. Special Uses of the Present Form\n\nBesides the use of the Present Form in indirect speech there are a number of special uses:\n\n1. Exhortations and pious formulas.\nGott sei Dank. — Thank God.\nEr lebe hoch. — Long may he live.\nSo sei es. — So be it.\n\n2. Recipes and directions.\nMan nehme 200 Gramm Mehl, zwei Eier … — Take 200 grams of flour, two eggs …\nMan denke dabei, dass … — Keep in mind that …\n\n3. Introductory phrases with the meaning of “let it (or us)” followed by the verb.\nEs sei noch einmal erwähnt, dass … — Let it be mentioned once more that …\nEs seien nur ein paar Tatsachen erwähnt. — Let us mention only a few facts.\n\n4. Mathematical and other formulas.\nDas Dreieck A – B – C sei dem Dreieck D – E – F gleich. — Let the triangle A‑B‑C be equal to the triangle D‑E‑F.\n"
      }
